Source revision: 18344a972d (local ../codex checkout)

Adapted files and algorithms:
- pycoder/agent.py, pycoder/history.py: core/src/session/turn.rs,
  core/src/compact.rs, core/src/session/mod.rs
- pycoder/patch.py: apply-patch/src/parser.rs, seek_sequence.rs, file_update.rs
- pycoder/prompts.py, pycoder/instructions/: models-manager/prompt.md,
  core/assets/tools/apply_patch.lark, core/src/tools/handlers/*_spec.rs,
  prompts/templates/compact/prompt.md, prompts/templates/compact/summary_prefix.md
- pycoder/util.py: byte-based token estimation and middle truncation concepts
- pycoder/tools.py: interfaces/semantics adapted from core/src/tools/handlers/
  request_user_input, shell, current_time, sleep, new_context_window, view_image
- pycoder/permissions.py: project-scoped approvals inspired by tools/orchestrator;
  exact command rules are a simplified implementation, not Codex execpolicy
- tests/fixtures: apply-patch/tests/fixtures/scenarios (selected scenarios)
- pycoder/tui.py, pycoder/tool_output.py: command display behavior inspired by
  tui/src/exec_cell/render.rs and live_output.rs (five-row previews, live tail,
  separate transcript); implemented independently with Textual and disk paging
- pycoder/team.py: local adaptation of lifecycle/mailbox concepts in
  core/src/tools/handlers/multi_agents_v2; one-level thread-based team, same provider
- pycoder/scheduler.py: parallel-safe tool dispatch with sequential mutation
  barriers, inspired by the Codex tool router
- pycoder/instructions/seatbelt*.sbpl: sandboxing/src/seatbelt_base_policy.sbpl
  and seatbelt_network_policy.sbpl, copied from the above revision. The generated
  policy and Python Bubblewrap/proxy/seccomp integration are project adaptations.

These files have been modified or translated for this standalone Python project.
No Ratatui code or other third-party runtime code from Codex is incorporated.
The standalone distribution separately includes Textual and its Python dependencies.
Their licenses and package metadata are included in their *.dist-info directories.
The original repository and its full NOTICE are available in ../codex.

This software is not an official OpenAI or Chutes product. It does not require
the Codex executable, OpenAI SDK, an OpenAI account, or OpenAI services.

Detailed instruction provenance and runtime adaptations: pycoder/instructions/SOURCES.md.
